From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MrLGamer <mrlgam3r@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] protonfixes: add DLSS 5 AMD OptiScaler downloader

A third-party experimental OptiScaler fork whose AMD path runs DLSS 5
Neural Rendering on a private HIP runtime before super resolution and at
render resolution, instead of after the upscale, i.e.

```
PROTON_ENABLE_DLSS5_AMD_OPTISCALER=1 %command%
```

Tracks the newest release, a tag instead of `1` pins one. Releases
carrying only a 7z are skipped: upstream stopped shipping them after
v1.6 and unpacking one needs a tool that is not a dependency here. A
release is deployed whole, which is what keeps the OptiScaler dll and
the pass dlls it SHA256-checks in step.

Everything lives in `system32/umu/dlss5_amd`, and WINE_OPTISCALER_DIR
points the loader at it, so it shares nothing with the OptiScaler
`setup_upscalers` deploys -- not the injected dll, not the ini, not the
companion libraries. The NGX snippet is staged into that folder too
rather than through the `dlss` flag, which installs into umu; without
one OptiScaler finds no nvngx, turns spoofing off, and the game never
offers DLSS for the pass to intercept. Turning it off leaves nothing
behind elsewhere and the folder can be deleted.

It refuses to activate rather than claim the injected dll for a pass that
cannot start: the runner must carry both the amdhip64_7 bridge and the
HIP runtime bundled beside it.
